{"text": "IN THE UNITED STATES DISTRICT COURT\nFOR THE WESTERN DISTRICT OF TEXAS\nSAN ANTONIO DIVISION\n\nESPERANZA G. MONTELONGO,                 §\n        Plaintiff,                         §\nv.                                         §     CIVIL ACTION NO. 5:25-cv-01183-XR\nHALVERSTON LOGISTICS GROUP, INC.,          §\n        Defendant.                         §\n\nPLAINTIFF'S ANSWERS TO DEFENDANT'S FIRST SET OF INTERROGATORIES\n\nTO: Defendant Halverston Logistics Group, Inc. (\"Halverston\" or \"HLG\"), through its counsel of record.\n\nUnder Fed. R. Civ. P. 33 and Local Rule CV-33, Plaintiff Esperanza Guadalupe Montelongo answers as\nfollows. Served March 6, 2026.\n\nGENERAL OBJECTIONS. Plaintiff objects to the extent any interrogatory seeks privileged\ncommunications (Fed. R. Evid. 501) or information outside Rule 26(b)(1). Subject to these\nobjections:\n\nINTERROGATORY NO. 1: State your full name, any other names used, date of birth, and\nthe last four digits of your Social Security number and your driver's license number.\nANSWER: Esperanza Guadalupe Montelongo. Before my marriage in 2014 I was Esperanza Guadalupe Rocha.\nCo-workers called me \"Espy.\" Born October 2, 1972 in Eagle Pass, Texas. SSN ends in\n7389. Texas driver's license 38841726 (Class A CDL until 2019, now Class C).\n\nINTERROGATORY NO. 2: Identify each address where you have lived in the past ten years.\nANSWER:\n  (a) 9114 Timber Path, Apt. 1206, San Antonio, TX 78250 - August 2024 to present.\n  (b) 417 W. Mayfield Blvd., San Antonio, TX 78221 - June 2017 to August 2024. This was the house\n      I owned with my husband, Rubén Montelongo. We sold it after I was fired.\n  (c) Rt. 3 Box 88-C, Pearsall, TX 78061 - 2014 to June 2017, my mother-in-law's property.\n\nINTERROGATORY NO. 3: Describe your education.\nANSWER: GED, 1991. Associate of Applied Science, Logistics Management, Palo Alto College,\nMay 2011 (student ID A00418827). No other degrees.\n\nINTERROGATORY NO. 4: Identify each employer for the past ten years, with dates, position,\nsupervisor and reason for leaving.\nANSWER:\n  (a) Halverston, Sunset Station terminal, 02/19/2018 to 11/08/2024. Night Dispatch Supervisor,\n      then Senior Dispatcher. Employee ID HL-041776. Supervisors: Dale Pustejovsky until 2022, then\n      Craig Vandenbosch, Regional Operations Manager. Terminated; the stated reason was\n      \"attendance.\" I contend the real reasons were my age, my religion and my illness.\n  (b) Pearsall Road Freight Brokers, LLC, March 2015 to Feb. 2018, dispatcher. Left for better pay.\n  (c) Yanaguana Staffing Solutions, temp assignments, Jan. 6, 2025 to 4/30/25, $17.50/hr.\n  (d) H-Town Carriers (remote), dispatcher, since May 12, 2025, $23.00 an hour, no benefits.\n  I was a member of Teamsters Local 657 while I drove (until 2019); I was not in the union as a supervisor.\n\nINTERROGATORY NO. 5: State each category of damages you claim and how it was computed.\nANSWER: Back pay: my 2023 Form W-2 from Halverston showed $78,442.16. From termination\nto the date of these answers I earned $31,905 in total, so lost wages are approximately\n$69,200 and continuing. Lost 401(k) match about $3,100 per year. COBRA premiums I paid: $1,142.77\na month for seven months. We lost roughly forty thousand dollars of equity selling the Mayfield\nhouse quickly. Compensatory damages for emotional distress in an amount for the jury.\nCounsel's fees under 42 U.S.C. § 2000e.\n\nINTERROGATORY NO. 6: Identify every health care provider who has treated you since\nJanuary 1, 2019.\nOBJECTION: overbroad as to conditions not at issue. Subject to that:\nANSWER:\n  (a) Dr. Evangeline Tso-Hartigan, Olmos Park Rheumatology Associates, 7950 Floyd Curl Dr., Ste. 410,\n      San Antonio - since September 2021 for systemic lupus erythematosus. Patient no. OP-0092214.\n  (b) Josefina Arriaga, LPC, Converse Counseling Collective, Converse, TX - weekly since Dec. 2024\n      for depression and anxiety following the termination.\n  (c) Dr. Harlan Niedermeyer, primary care, about twice a year.\n  (d) Emergency room, July 4, 2023, lupus flare with chest pain; I missed two shifts. Halverston\n      counted both as unexcused although I gave Mr. Vandenbosch the discharge papers.\n\nINTERROGATORY NO. 7: Identify each medication you took during your employment.\nANSWER: Hydroxychloroquine 200 mg twice daily; prednisone tapers during flares; since December 2024,\nsertraline 50 mg. I asked Lakeisha Prudhomme, HR Business Partner, for a day-shift transfer as an\naccommodation on August 14, 2023 and again by email on 9/22/23. Ms. Prudhomme never answered\nin writing.\n\nINTERROGATORY NO. 8: State whether you have been a party to any other lawsuit, claim,\ncharge, bankruptcy, or criminal proceeding.\nANSWER: EEOC Charge No. 451-2025-00817, filed 01/22/2025; right-to-sue notice July 30, 2025.\nUnemployment claim with the state workforce commission (TWC), granted over Halverston's protest.\nChapter 7 bankruptcy with my husband in 2016, Case No. 16-51407-cag, discharged. In 1994 I received\ndeferred adjudication for misdemeanor theft in Bexar County (cause no. CR-94-3381) under\nPenal Code § 31.03; dismissed after probation. No other proceedings.\n\nINTERROGATORY NO. 9: Identify each financial account into which your wages were deposited\nand each credit account on which you claim to have incurred debt because of the termination.\nOBJECTION: invasive and disproportionate. Subject to that, and to the protective order:\nANSWER: Wages went to Bexar Frontier Credit Union, checking xxxxxx4093 (routing 111193563). After\nthe firing I ran up my Bexar Frontier Visa, 4426 0853 5406 7042, to $11,870, and a Mastercard ending\n8039 to its $6,500 limit. Both cards are in my name alone. I will produce statements\nunder Rule 33(d), Bates MONTELONGO-000118 to -000204.\n\nINTERROGATORY NO. 10: Identify each motor vehicle you owned or leased since 2022.\nANSWER: 2020 Chevrolet Equinox, Texas plate RKT-4471, VIN 3GNAXKEV4LS508216, financed by\nMesquite Flats Auto Finance, loan MFA-2209-77314. It was repossessed March 3, 2025. I now drive my\nhusband's 2011 Ford F-150, plate BXJ 2087.\n\nINTERROGATORY NO. 11: Identify each device, phone number, email account and social media\naccount you used to communicate about your employment.\nANSWER: Personal phone, Samsung Galaxy S23, number (210) 555-0149, IMEI 353809935256419. Halverston-issued\nlaptop, Dell Latitude 5440, asset tag HLG-LT-03392, returned 11/11/2024. Email:\nespy.montelongo72@correo.example and my work address emontelongo@halverstonlogistics.example. Facebook\nprofile under my name; LinkedIn linkedin.example/in/esperanza-montelongo-sa. I posted nothing about the\ncompany. My login to the dispatch TMS was EMONTELONGO2; I do not have the password.\n\nINTERROGATORY NO. 12: Identify each person with knowledge of the facts alleged.\nANSWER: Mr. Vandenbosch; Ms. Prudhomme; Mr. Pustejovsky; my husband Rubén, 210-555-0102;\nMarisela Cantú, former day dispatcher, who heard Vandenbosch say on or about October 17, 2024 that\nhe needed \"younger legs on nights\" - Ms. Cantú lives in Schertz, 210.555.0187;\nPastor Elwood Gittens-Simms of Brooks City Seventh-day Adventist Church, who wrote\nthe letter of June 3, 2024 explaining why I cannot work from Friday sundown to Saturday sundown.\n\nINTERROGATORY NO. 13: State the basis for your claim of religious discrimination.\nANSWER: I am a Seventh-day Adventist and have kept the Sabbath since my baptism in 2009. For six\nyears Mr. Pustejovsky scheduled around it. In April 2024 Mr. Vandenbosch put me on\nrotating Saturdays. I used vacation for 9 Saturdays, then was written up on 8/31/24,\n9/28/24 and 10/26/24, each a Saturday. Two younger supervisors, both under 40, were given\nfixed weekday schedules. I was 52 when I was terminated and the oldest dispatcher at the terminal.\n\nVERIFICATION\nI declare under penalty of perjury under 28 U.S.C. § 1746 that the foregoing answers are\ntrue and correct. Executed in Bexar County, Texas, on March 5, 2026.\n\n                                   /s/ Esperanza G. Montelongo\n\nAs to objections:\nThaddeus Okpewho (State Bar No. 24098817)\nOKPEWHO & STRADLING, PLLC\n310 S. St. Mary's Street, Suite 1450\nSan Antonio, Texas 78205\nTel. 210-555-0131 / Fax 210-555-0132\ntokpewho@okpewhostradling.example\nAttorney for Plaintiff. Our file OS-25-0214.", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "1,215 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["ESPERANZA G. MONTELONGO", "Rubén Montelongo", "Halverston", "Pearsall Road Freight Brokers", "Yanaguana Staffing Solutions", "H-Town Carriers", "Dr. Evangeline Tso-Hartigan", "Josefina Arriaga", "Dr. Harlan Niedermeyer", "Lakeisha Prudhomme", "Esperanza G. Montelongo", "Mr. Vandenbosch", "Ms. Prudhomme", "Mr. Pustejovsky", "Rubén", "Marisela Cantú", "Pastor Elwood Gittens-Simms", "Thaddeus Okpewho"], "companies": ["Halverston Logistics Group", "HLG", "Halverston", "Pearsall Road Freight Brokers, LLC", "Yanaguana Staffing Solutions", "H-Town Carriers, LLC", "Olmos Park Rheumatology Associates", "Converse Counseling Collective", "Hydroxychloroquine", "Prednisone", "EEOC", "TWC", "Bexar Frontier Credit Union", "Mesquite Flats Auto Finance", "Chevrolet", "Ford", "Halverston Logistics", "Brooks City Seventh-day Adventist Church", "OKPEWHO & STRADLING, PLLC"]}, "chunks": 4, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.19999999925494194, "modelMs": 84947.19999999925, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names"], "detections": [{"start": 70, "end": 81, "text": "SAN ANTONIO", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "San Antonio"}, {"start": 92, "end": 115, "text": "ESPERANZA G. MONTELONGO", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "ESPERANZA G. MONTELONGO"}, 